       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg per day. That is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4 g per day, and some institutions cap it at 3 g per day. A dose that high risks serious liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg per day.\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg per day.\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the intended order with your resident or attending, and with pharmacy if you're unsure."
