       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Nine grams of acetaminophen a day could cause acute liver failure, and a patient with normal liver function is still at risk. I can't treat a confirmation from a student as clinical verification of a dose this far above the safe maximum.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g per day) or 650 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2.6 g per day).\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If they want a dose above the standard limit, they can enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably review it too.\n- **Look at the units.** If 3000 mg was meant as the daily total, I can enter it as divided doses.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
